{
  "version": "4.1",
  "stop_time": "10",
  "dt": "0.001",
  "backend": "python",
  "variables": {
    "M": "0.5",
    "m": "0.2",
    "b": "0.1",
    "l": "0.3",
    "I": "0.006",
    "g": "9.8"
  },
  "description": "Nonlinear cart-pendulum, CTMS four-Fcn form with an algebraic loop through the interaction forces N and P.",
  "provenance": "CTMS, Inverted Pendulum: Simulink Modeling, https://ctms.engin.umich.edu/CTMS/?example=InvertedPendulum&section=SimulinkModeling . Equations (1), (2), (13) and (14) of that page, one Fcn block each: x'' = (F - N - b x')/M, theta'' = (-N l cos(theta) - P l sin(theta))/I, N = m(x'' - l theta'^2 sin(theta) + l theta'' cos(theta)), P = m(l theta'^2 cos(theta) + l theta'' sin(theta) + g). x'' and theta'' feed N and P, which feed x'' and theta'' back: an algebraic loop solved by Newton on the loop-cut signals at every evaluation, as Simulink does. Parameters, theta(0)=pi and the 1 N s impulse (Pulse Generator 1000 N, period 10 s, width 0.01 %) are those of mwe_inverted_pendulum.json, which solves the same equations explicitly.",
